From 407056b21d8b90a8e1ad191fdba46d2c8cbe9254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: s1oplus <victorgarcez@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] grate: one-pass wlroots programs, RGBX as its own
 program

The premultiplied "over" programs took two passes through the fragment
pipeline (sample and multiply, then fetch the destination and blend).
PSEQ fetches the destination pixel at the start of an EXEC and TEX runs
after the interpolation in the same EXEC, so do both in one pass: the
texel goes to r0,r1, the destination to r2,r3, and two ALU steps compute
dst * (1 - src.a * alpha) + src * alpha (alpha via the "r3.h - 1"
operand). Solid "over" gets 1 - colour.a from the CPU in u2.l.

The per-pixel red/blue swap selects are gone: grate only samples
B8G8R8A8/X8 into B8G8R8A8/X8 targets, so they never swapped. RGBX
textures get their own programs instead of a per-pixel select.

Full-screen 1280x800: copy 9.3 -> 5.4 ms, over 18 -> 8.5 ms,
solid 5.8 -> 3.7 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
